   397	  the attention bench (eight cases, model-layout ratios established), the
   398	  boundary bench (terminal status per registered chain) and its qualified
   399	  trace analysis; both sessions: manifest, collection summary, reference
   400	  lineage (directory marker and every sidecar), clock log, and every
   401	  auxiliary terminal record OK — and writes the mechanical session verdict
   402	  (COMPLETE / INCOMPLETE with per-item reasons) to `session_status.json`.
   403	  Collection and the audit are themselves supervised; a previous verdict is
   404	  invalidated before every finalisation and any collection or audit failure
   405	  or timeout writes an explicit INCOMPLETE; every measurement or trace
   406	  attempt invalidates its own previous artifacts (run JSON, report, exports,
   407	  derived reductions) before it starts, so no stale success can survive a
   408	  failed attempt. Every on-pod reduction (nsys
   409	  exports, graph verification, timing views, ideal costs, perturbation) is
   410	  bounded by the session deadline, invalidates its stale outputs before the
   411	  attempt (the main-trace reductions belong to the `trace` attempt only;
   412	  perturbation traces invalidate their own products), even when the attempt
   413	  is then skipped for the deadline, and leaves a terminal `aux_<name>.json`
