   459	  boundary microbench (§4) plus its node-level trace and traced-vs-unprofiled
   460	  perturbation; per-kernel ideal costs (plan 1.4) computed only from the
   461	  compiled variant(s) whose ORDERED per-pass Triton sequence is reproduced
   462	  by a UNIQUE decomposition into compiled-graph call sequences (graphs may
   463	  repeat; graphs are interchangeable only when their complete pricing
   464	  semantics agree — kernel body hashes, access sites, iteration literals,
   465	  argument shapes/strides/types and every extern/fallback call in order; graphs without Triton kernels are invisible to the
   466	  decomposition and are stated as such; SDPA call count reconciled exactly,
   467	  GEMM events ≥ extern calls, captured pass count = 50; zero or several
   468	  decompositions → UNRESOLVED, expected for graph-broken arms such as C1/C2
   469	  whose per-graph kernel numbering makes names non-unique). Inductor GEMM
   470	  template kernels (`triton_tem_*`, max-autotune) are counted in the GEMM
   471	  class and are not priced by the byte model. Registered deviations from a literal
   472	  per-kernel FLOPs/bytes table: cuBLAS kernel names carry no shapes, so GEMM
   473	  ideals are computed per extern call site from the wrapper and compared at
   474	  class level; SDPA ideals are class-level (12 calls/pass at the model
   475	  shapes); Inductor fused pointwise/reduction kernels are priced by bytes
   476	  only (bandwidth bound, zero FLOPs) with per-call L2 residency tests. Byte
   477	  model for a fused kernel call: per pointer argument, element size from the
   478	  kernel's own ABI signature (`triton_meta`), traffic = min(distinct
   479	  elements of the argument's strided footprint, load/store sites × the
   480	  call's iteration space) × element size, reads and writes charged
   481	  separately, where the iteration space is the product of the call's
   482	  positional integer literals bound one-to-one to the kernel's numeric
   483	  parameters (any other call form is UNRESOLVED); the L2 residency test
   484	  uses the union of the distinct base allocations the call touches, each at
   485	  its full allocated size (an over-estimate: a call passes the test only
   486	  when its whole working set provably fits — allocation size is the address
   487	  extent from the base allocation's own shape, stride and dtype, unknown →
   488	  no L2 ideal); every measured value comes from exactly 50 non-empty
   489	  validated per-pass windows (the aggregate kernel summary is reconciled
   490	  against them by name set, count and duration, and the numerical
   491	  discrepancy is always reported), and an ideal-cost run whose requested or
   492	  observed pass count is not the registered 50 publishes an explicit
   493	  UNREGISTERED_PROTOCOL record with no rows; wrapper calls the parser does
   494	  not recognise (assigned or not, any `torch.ops` namespace) are recorded
   495	  verbatim and make graphs non-interchangeable; boundary calibration
   496	  derives the expected dependency counter from N, mode, warm-up and
   497	  repeats and requires both recorded counters to equal it;
   498	  boundary calibration accepts a segment only when its case carries a passed
   499	  dependency-proof counter (trivial chains) and, for PDL modes, the PTX
   500	  qualification — labels alone never qualify; source-map coverage credits
   501	  only exact, unambiguous kernel names with resolved fused ops; graph-input dtypes from the wrapper's benchmark section;
   502	  fallback-op outputs from their `assert_size_stride`. This over-counts
   503	  slice reads, so a row whose HBM-model ideal exceeds its measured time is
   504	  flagged `bound_not_tight` and its recoverable share under the HBM model is
   505	  0 (never negative, never inflated); eager ATen fallbacks, cuFFT and copy
   506	  kernels without wrapper shapes stay UNRESOLVED. A kernel → fused-op source
   507	  map with its coverage share accompanies the table; exports; evidence
   508	  extraction. Session 2 runs under the
   509	  same deadline/reserve/terminal-record rules as session 1 (qualification
   510	  and microbenchmarks included).
   511	  **Plan 1.7 dependency model (registered):** the exports carry no event or
   512	  graph edges, so the critical-path view is the OBSERVED-ORDER longest chain
   513	  of pairwise non-overlapping kernels (edge a→b iff a ended before b
   514	  started); it is an upper bound on the true dependency path, satisfies
   515	  `critical_path ≤ union ≤ span` by construction (asserted), and is labelled
   516	  as such; the union and the summed views are exact.
   517	- Engineering shakedown of the harness on ml-beast GPU 4 is permitted before
   518	  session 1 (the `sm120` smoke rule): its outputs are never session evidence
   519	  and are never cited.
   520	- Budget guard: every process runs under `timeout`; a timed-out or crashed
   521	  run is INVALID/UNTESTED in its JSON and the session continues (loud in the
   522	  console log, never silent).
